.TH mkfs.briefs 8

.SH NAME
.PP
mkfs.briefs - Create a new BrieFS filesystem


.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
mkfs.briefs

.PP
.RS

.nf
[--block-size|-b]=[value]
[--force|-f]
[--help|-h]
[--inode-ratio]=[value]
[--inode-size|-I]=[value]
[--journal-size|-j]=[value]
[--label|-L]=[value]
[--size|-s]=[value]
[--uuid|-U]=[value]
[--version|-v]

.fi
.RE


.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Create a new BrieFS filesystem on DEVICE.  BrieFS is an extents-and-tries Linux filesystem.  mkfs.briefs writes the on-disk v0.9.0 format: a packed directory-trie layout, a B+ tree extent index for files with more than eight extents, and a user_flags inode field exposing chattr/lsattr flags (sync, dirsync, immutable, append-only, nodump, noatime).

.PP
\fBUsage\fP:

.PP
.RS

.nf
mkfs.briefs [global options] DEVICE

.fi
.RE


.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.PP
\fB--block-size, -b\fP="": block size in bytes (default: 4096)

.PP
\fB--force, -f\fP: force overwrite of an existing filesystem

.PP
\fB--help, -h\fP: show help

.PP
\fB--inode-ratio\fP="": blocks per inode (one inode per N blocks) (default: 8)

.PP
\fB--inode-size, -I\fP="": inode size in bytes (default: 512)

.PP
\fB--journal-size, -j\fP="": journal size in blocks (0 = auto: scale with volume size) (default: 0)

.PP
\fB--label, -L\fP="": filesystem label (default: "BRIEFS")

.PP
\fB--size, -s\fP="": filesystem size in blocks (default: 0)

.PP
\fB--uuid, -U\fP="": Specify a UUID for the new volume.

.PP
\fB--version, -v\fP: print the version
